      "outputs": [],
      "title": "How image to 3D works",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Image to 3D: Hyper3D Gen2 vs Hitem3D 2.0\n\n1. Seedream draws one object on a plain background. Replace the prompt, or swap in **Load Image** with your own picture of a single object.\n2. Both models build a textured 3D model from that same image, so you can compare them side by side.\n3. Open each result in its **Save 3D (Advanced)** viewer; use the export button to download another format. GLB copies are saved to the ComfyUI output folder.\n\nFor better results use one clear object, centered, on a plain background. Hitem3D accepts up to four views (front, back, left, right): connect an image batch and set **views**. **1536pro** is the second resolution option.\n\nNeeds a ModelArk key in Settings > BytePlus. Each generation is billed."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": ""
      },
